            <ArticleTitle>Brain parenchymal, subarachnoid racemose, and intraventricular cysticercosis in an Indian man.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>164-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The coexistence of brain parenchymal cysts at various stages of evolution, both intraventricular and subarachnoid racemose, is reported in a patient with neurocysticercosis. The condition has a variety of presentations, depending on the location of the cyst. This case is of particular interest because of the rarity of this condition in India.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
